WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.480
The track team was really just a big family.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.870
Brothers and sisters and the coaches are your
parents, keeping you in line.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:20.080
We would travel together, spend close to 40
hours a week together.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:21.670
The track team was very large.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.009
I think we had about 40 guys and the same
amount of women.

00:00:26.009 --> 00:00:29.270
We'd travel to meets with 60 or 70 athletes.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:34.660
We'd bring to a national meet, we brought
probably 15 guys and 15 girls.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:39.730
Yeah, my relationship with Coach Lumberg was
really strong.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:44.310
He recruited me to Hillsdale, but he's a distance
coach, cross country coach.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:50.060
We have a field events coach who was going
to be my coach, it's Coach Teft.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.960
He's really the one who was able to mold me
into the athlete that I became.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.650
We spent a lot of time together, but there's
a lot of trust that has to happen.

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:02.050
I trust what they're doing.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.630
Thank goodness Coach Teft had a lot of experience.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:10.479
He would give me all the advice that I needed
to change my workouts or keep them the same

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:12.770
or change my steps.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:18.630
It was a great working relationship, because
these guys are so easy to get to know, easy

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:23.560
to work with and they just love everyone they
work with, as long as you're willing to put

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:25.350
in the work and the time.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:32.390
The success that I had as a collegiate athlete
was coupled with failures as well.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:37.520
The failures that I had were mostly during
the season trying different things, but it

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:44.940
was an experiment that Coach Teft and I and
Coach Lundberg were working to figure out,

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:50.310
what was going to be the best to prepare me
for the big dance, which is the Nationals.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.970
In my freshman year, I was fifth in the country
in the high-jump.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:02:00.920
I have eight times as an All American, I feel
like I represent the teams of the early '90's.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:06.170
We had a great string from '91, '92, '93,
'94.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:11.009
We lost the first year of the GLIAC championship,
but we never lost after that.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:17.999
I represent Coach Teft, Coach Lundberg, Coach
Martha, and I'm just the guy who gets to get

00:02:17.999 --> 00:02:20.569
inducted for the Hall of Fame for them.

00:02:20.569 --> 00:02:23.280
I just feel like I'm their representative.

